# What clasp is allowed to push into the Apps Script project.
#
# Deny everything, then name the backend. This file exists because of an outage:
# `apps-script/test/` arrived with no ignore rules, so `clasp push` sent the Node
# test files to Google along with the sources. Their first line is
# `require('node:test')`, and Apps Script runs the top level of every file in the
# project on every single request — so every call died with
# "ReferenceError: require is not defined" before reaching doPost, the web app
# answered an HTML error page, and the browser turned that into
# `TypeError: Failed to fetch`. The app was unopenable and none of it was in the
# app.
#
# Default-deny rather than a list of exclusions: the next thing added next to the
# sources — a tool, a fixture, a second test folder — is then out by default
# instead of quietly ending up in production. Adding a real backend file means
# adding it here, and `verify` fails if a pushed file is not one Apps Script can
# run.
**/**
!*.js
!appsscript.json
